# Origin of the API, including the /api/v1 prefix.
#
# BAKED IN AT BUILD TIME, not read at runtime. Vite substitutes `import.meta.env.*`
# into the bundle during `vite build`, so this value is frozen into the deployed
# artifact. Two consequences worth knowing before debugging a "wrong API" report:
#
#   1. Changing it on the hosting platform does nothing until the app is REBUILT.
#      Redeploying the existing build serves the old value.
#   2. It has to exist in the BUILD environment, not only the runtime one.
#
# Left unset, the build falls back to this localhost default and the deployed app
# calls an API that does not exist from the visitor's browser — with no server-side
# error anywhere, because those requests never reach a server.
#
# Keep three values consistent, or auth and mailed links break in ways that do not
# announce themselves:
#   - this VITE_API_URL          -> the API origin
#   - the API's CORS_ORIGINS     -> this app's origin (cookies need an exact match)
#   - the API's WEB_APP_URL      -> this app's origin (every mailed link is built from it)
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1
